Independent value-operation and E820 verification

Authored fragments: selfhost/x64-values.zero.part, ia32-values.zero.part,
real-values.zero.part, real-memmap.zero.part. No assembler or linker used.
Fragments were decoded by our own Zero program and inspected with read-only
objdump; every instruction and branch target matched its specified ABI.

Native host, raw x64 BIOS VM, and raw IA32 BIOS VM passed110 mathematical
assertions:60 shifts and50 XOR/AND cases. Shift boundaries include0,1,7,31,
32,33,63,64,65,0xffffffff,0x100000000 and maximumu64, applied to zero, one,
maximumu64, the high bit, and a mixed-bit pattern. IA32 VM disabled long mode
and PAE. Both VMs exited through debug-exit with status1 and exact success
marker THREADS OK (the existing generic VM fixture protocol).

Host positional I/O passed FD3 offset8 write/read roundtrip, EOF, EBADF,
and verification that pread/pwrite do not change the descriptor's current
position. Host FD3 is opened read/write on an initial24-byte file containing
START---................ and duplicated to stdin for cursor checks.
The persistent native fixture also includes fsync success/EBADF assertions;
the compiler parent independently verified those on the full candidate.

Standalone real-mode probe passed90 u32 bit/shift assertions and complete
BIOS E820 enumeration through continuation0. It checked returned sizes20..24,
at least one nonempty usable-RAM record, a local-frame canary, buffer+28
canary, and invalid buffers0xffe1/0xffffffff returning0xffffffff. Probe size
9592 bytes. Only the16KiB BIOS image at ISO LBA32 was replaced in the frozen
/workspace/zero-snapshot-0.6.0/build/zero.iso. QEMU qemu64,-lm,-pae,128MiB,
SeaBIOS printed exact VALUES E820 OK and exited with expected status1.

No current operating-system artifact or canonical compiler was changed by
these probes. Persistent source fixtures are in review-tests/compiler-fs.
The x64/IA32 and real VM output, kernel/boot binaries and QEMU logs are saved
in the neighboring x64-vm, ia32-vm and real-vm directories.
